we begin this morning with what one  military official is calling a miracle a  charter flight with a hundred  forty-three people on board slid off a  runway at Naval Air Station Jacksonville  in Florida and into a river but everyone  on board made it off alive and in good  condition the Navy says the Boeing 737  was carrying military personnel and  civilians from the US naval base at  Guantanamo Bay Cuba some of the  passengers were scheduled to travel on  to other naval bases from Jacksonville  the plane came to a stop in a shallow  part of the st. Johns River with a  half-hour dozens of military civilian  rescuers were on the scene some making  their way to the plane by boat  our crews went in the water immediately  to the wing edge and started escorting  people that were on the wing edge to the  shore 21 people were taken to hospitals  with minor injuries cleanup crews are  working this morning to contain the jet  fuel that is leaking into the river  there's no word on what caused the plane  to end up in the river and there was  stormy weather in the area at the time  federal air safety investigators are due  in Jacksonville today
 

